<% content_for :title, "About" %>
<article class="about-page narrow">
  <h1>About Commonbound</h1>
  <p>In 2013, we met while building somewhere.com, a place to find somewhere you fit. We were trying to rethink how people find their place in the world of work, and how work could become something more meaningful than simply earning a living.</p>
  <p>We eventually ran out of funding and went our separate ways, but our conversations about work, its culture and how it shapes our world never stopped.</p>
  <p>Thirteen years later, we’re back.</p>
  <p>Building Commonbound: a platform to reshape the way we talk about work, purpose and our personal impact on the world. We want to make it easier for people to discover the problems they care about, find organisations working towards similar goals and connect with others who want to contribute to something bigger.</p>
  <p>Because we believe your professional identity is about more than your job title. And your contribution to society is about more than your pay cheque.</p>
  <p>We think it’s time to change the narrative. And we’re building Commonbound to help make that happen.</p>
  <h2>Nika van Olst</h2>
  <p>As a sustainability strategist and ecosystem builder, Nika works at the intersection of people, purpose and systemic change. She’s interested in how we bring people together around shared challenges, how we turn ambitious ideas into collective action, and how we create the conditions for positive change to happen.</p>
  <p>Her work is driven by a question that keeps coming back: how do we make it easier for people to contribute to a world they want to be part of?</p>
  <p>For Nika, sustainability has never been just about reducing harm or ticking boxes. It’s about rethinking the systems we operate in, questioning what we consider progress and finding new ways to collaborate on the problems that matter.</p>
